"Sets the PQC enforcement policy.\n"
"\n"
"`STRICT`: a connection will be refused unless both the client and the server support a PQC-capable group (`X25519MLKEM768`, `SecP256r1MLKEM768`, `SecP384r1MLKEM1024`). The server requires PQC-capable clients.\n"
"\n"
"`CLIENT_NEGOTIATED`: the server advertises PQC groups but will not refuse a connection if the client does not support them, allowing fallback to classical key exchange.\n"
"\n"
"`RELAXED`: no PQC enforcement; standard TLS key exchange negotiation applies.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:+++QUARKUS_TLS_PQC_ENFORCEMENT_POLICY+++[]\n"
